                    <h4 class="title">Overview</h4>
                    <p class="meta">Populary known as <a href="#" style="text-decoration: none; color: chocolate;">Hindu Pilgrimage Festival</a></p>

                    <p>Kumbh Mela is the largest religious gathering in the world. Millions of devotees, saints, and pilgrims gather to take a holy dip in sacred rivers during astrologically significant dates.</p>
                    
                    <h3>Mythological Background</h3>
                    <p>The festival is based on the legend of Samudra Manthan (churning of the ocean). 
                        It is believed that drops of the divine nectar (amrit) fell at four locations — which are now the Kumbh Mela sites.</p>
                    <h5>Major Rituals</h5>
<ul style="list-style-type: square; padding-left: 20px;">
    <li>Shahi Snan (Royal Bath): The most significant ritual where sadhus and devotees take a dip in the river.</li>
    <li>Processions: Grand processions of sadhus, saints, and devotees with music and chanting.</li>
    <li>Religious Discourses: Spiritual leaders and gurus deliver sermons and teachings.</li>
</ul>
                    
                    <h5>Logistical Scale</h5>
                   
                    <ul style="list-style-type: square; padding-left: 20px;">
                        <li>A temporary city is constructed with roads, bridges, hospitals, security systems, and sanitation facilities.</li>
                        <li>Advanced crowd control, drone surveillance, and disaster management systems are deployed.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <h5>Significance</h5>
                    <ul style="list-style-type: square; padding-left: 20px;">
                        <li>Recognized by UNESCO as Intangible Cultural Heritage..</li>
